# What `gcloud run deploy --source .` may upload to Cloud Build (7.8.4).
# .dockerignore only filters inside the build; this decides what leaves this
# machine at all. data/ holds scraped vacancies AND personal files (CVs,
# labels, runs) -- in a worktree it is a link to the real data -- and .env
# holds secrets: neither is ever uploaded. `gcloud meta list-files-for-upload`
# shows exactly what would go.
#
# Folder rules start with "/": without it a rule matches at every depth, and
# "web/" or "evals/" would also drop src/joblens/web and src/joblens/evals,
# which the app imports (caught by counting src's files before a deploy).
.gcloudignore
.env
.env.*
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
/data
/.git
/.gitignore
/.claude/
/.venv/
/.ruff_cache/
/.pytest_cache/
/tests/
/docs/
/evals/
/web/
/docker/
/compose.yaml
/boards.toml
/sources.toml
/CLAUDE.md
/.python-version
# Of the scripts, only the hosted start is part of the image.
/scripts/*
!/scripts/hosted.py
